package "main"

// exec.divergence (the "mode-dependent FORM of a defined abort" kind) +
// exec.contract.scope (such a form is OUTSIDE the result-agreement): some
// DEFINED non-recoverable panics (§17.5) have an observable FORM that is
// mode/target dependent even though the FACT of the abort is guaranteed. The
// canonical example is dispatching through a NIL interface value
// (iface.dispatch.nil, §11.11): in COMPILED native code it is a silent fault on
// the null-vtable dereference -- the program prints "before" and then stops,
// never reaching "after". The VM-mode FORM (a recoverable "runtime error: call of
// nil interface value" fault) is pinned separately by 11-interfaces/082, and on a target
// with no memory protection the deref may not fault at all (the arm32-baremetal
// xfail). So the two forms are pinned by separate per-mode tests; this is the
// compiled form.
//
// (The positive harness compares stdout only -- it does not capture the exit
// signal -- so the OBSERVABLE asserted here is that execution stops before
// "after"; the FACT of the abort follows from the silent null-vtable fault, and
// the VM form (082) pins the abort explicitly via its diagnostic.)
interface I {
	foo()
}

type T struct {
	x int
}

func (t *T) foo() {
	println("foo")
}

impl *T : I

func main() {
	println("before")
	var iv *I
	iv.foo()
	println("after")
}
